    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> kingdom founded around 1500 by the Luo-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babito-dynasty">Babito dynasty</a>, which claimed the heritage of ancient Kitara.</li><li>Its salt and iron made it rich, and in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries its armies dominated the region.</li><li>Omukama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a> rebuilt its power but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1899; Bunyoro is today a cultural kingdom.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a> was captured in 1899 together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwanga-ii">Mwanga</a>, the deposed king of Buganda, a long-time rival who had become his ally; the British exiled both men to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

